-- title:
--   Finite envelopes certify every shared-bank resource obligation
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J,N_B,N_C,g,n,f,d$ be natural numbers with $N_B,N_C\le n$. Write $E(h,J,n)$ for the shared-bank allocation envelope, $W(h,J,n,g)$ for its explicit numeric envelope, and $D(h,J)=512h+\operatorname{levels}(J)+2(512hJ)+30$ for its depth allowance. For machine limits $(S,V,L)$, assume
--   $$
--   f+E(h,J,n)\le S,\qquad W(h,J,n,g)\le V,\qquad d+D(h,J)\le L.
--   $$
--   Then the shared reporting host's full resource certificate holds at base $f$ and call depth $d$. Its fields bound total storage, control values, source-bank spans, powers, local pairs, depth computation, and every nested reporting-level constructor. The envelopes include headers, retained catalogs, packed indices, and construction scratch.
--
--   This packages the detailed constructor obligations into three finite inequalities.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/SharedReportingBankResourceBounds.lean#L129-L203

